17;s async-profiler or Java Flight Recorder operates at 100 Hz sampling to ca=
pture execution traces, memory allocation rates, and thread lock contention. =
Python&#8217;s py-spy provides low-overhead, async stack sampling of live pro=
duction processes. Go has pprof, which generates goroutine profiles, heap sna=
pshots, and block contention data.</p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: r=
gb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">Each=
 one of these profilers breaks down execution into call stacks. They track tw=
o main metrics. First, you have the inclusive time. This is the total time sp=
ent executing a function. It includes every child function and the subroutine=
s called by this function. Second, you have the Self (CPU) Time. It&#8217;s t=
he time spent running code purely inside the function itself. No external cal=
ls are involved.</p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-=
height: 26px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">With this exercise, th=
e Netflix engineering team came to the conclusion that a single analytical pi=
peline could understand data from almost any programming runtime.</p><p style=
=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-size: 16px=
;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">Another advantage of LLMs is that they don&#8217;t=
 have to guess how an algorithm works from scratch. Since LLMs have been broa=
dly trained on many software repositories, they are mostly familiar with clas=
sic programming anti-patterns. For example, they know that quadratic loops wh=
ere a hot method is called again and again for each item in a collection aren=
&#8217;t a good idea. Also, loop invariants where you compute a calculation f=
or every iteration of the loop instead of making the calculation once at the =
beginning. Other patterns include excessive object allocation on hot executio=
n paths and &#8220;N+1&#8221; query patterns.</p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px=
 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plain=
text;">Due to this knowledge base of LLMs, you don&#8217;t need to ask an AI =
model to guess why an application might be performing poorly. You can build a=
 workflow that asks the model to pattern-match known performance bugs against=
 actual call stacks.</p><h2 class=3D"header-anchor-post" style=3D"position: r=
elative;font-family: 'SF Pro Display',-apple-system-headline,system-ui,-apple=
