ibility;appearance: optimizelegibility;margin: 1em 0 0.625em 0;color: rgb(54,=
55,55);line-height: 1.16em;font-size: calc(1.625em * 1);overflow-wrap: anywhe=
re;word-break: normal;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">Safety, Verification, and Tru=
st Architecture</h2><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-=
height: 26px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">If you have an AI agen=
t that can optimize code, it&#8217;s quite dangerous if the changes are appli=
ed without automatic verification. If the agent makes a change that breaks bu=
siness logic, it&#8217;s worse than inefficient code.</p><p style=3D"margin: =
0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bid=
i: plaintext;">To prevent regressions, the agentic pipeline uses the standard=
 SDLC.</p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26=
px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">In stage 1, you verify the logic=
. Before you move any code, the agent&#8217;s branch must pass all existing u=
nit, integration, and contract tests. This is to make sure that the changes m=
ade by the change don&#8217;t alter basic inputs, outputs, or handling of edg=
e cases.</p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: =
26px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">In stage 2, you have the canar=
y deployment. If the tests pass, the pipeline spins up a canary deployment in=
 production. The canary instance gets a portion of the traffic. It runs side-=
by-side with an identical baseline instance that runs the original code.</p><=
p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-siz=
e: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">Stage 3 is about generating the observabili=
ty report. The platform collects hard telemetry metrics over a big enough win=
dow. Some metrics are relative CPU utilization, median latency, P99 latency, =
and memory allocation rates. They also don&#8217;t use any AI model to check =
the canary results.</p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);li=
ne-height: 26px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">In stage 4, you hav=
e the final engineering decision. When the canary version shows a good level =
of performance improvement with zero increase in error rates, the system open=
s a PR. This PR goes for human review. It includes the code change, the origi=
nal flame graph, and the canary report. The final decision on deploying the c=
hange to production is taken by the human developer.</p><h2 class=3D"header-a=
nchor-post" style=3D"position: relative;font-family: 'SF Pro Display',-apple-=
system-headline,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,=
