: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 1.16em;font-size: calc(1.625em * 1);overflow-wra=
p: anywhere;word-break: normal;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">Shifting Left</h2><p=
 style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-size=
: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">Automated production profiling is quite effe=
ctive. But if you just rely on it, you end up exposing several limitations.</=
p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-=
size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">By the time an agent finds an anti-patte=
rn in production, you&#8217;ve already paid for days or weeks of wasted compu=
te capacity.</p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-heig=
ht: 26px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">Second, developers are any=
way cautious about changing a running service. If you have a service that han=
dles production traffic without crashing, the developers hesitate to just mak=
e changes for the sake of optimization.</p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;col=
or: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;"=
>Lastly, multiple teams often make the exact same mistakes when it comes to p=
atterns. If you run a super-expensive agent on 10 different services just to =
find the same problem, it&#8217;s not very efficient.</p><p style=3D"margin: =
0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bid=
i: plaintext;">These limitations led to Netflix making the decision to shift =
performance checks left into the early development cycle. Also, they wanted t=
he agents to share their findings across the entire engineering organization.=
</p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;fon=
t-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">However, as you might know, language m=
odels are stateless. Every time you send a prompt to an LLM, it starts with a=
 clean slate. It might no retain any memory of the bug it found some time bac=
k in another service. The Netflix engineering team built a Pattern Catalog to=
 make the models achieve persistence. This was done by pairing a stateless LL=
M with a stateful catalog. Or a shared memory across the fleet.</p><p style=
=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-size: 16px=
;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">The Pattern Catalog was built around 4 key princip=
les.</p><ul style=3D"margin-top: 0;padding: 0;"><li style=3D"margin: 8px 0 0 =
32px;mso-special-format: bullet;unicode-bidi: plaintext;"><p style=3D"color: =
rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;margin-bottom: 0;box-sizing: border-box;paddi=
ng-left: 4px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;margin: 0;">First, it ha=
s to be centralized and serve as the single source of truth for all engineeri=
ng teams. This way, no two teams end up debugging the same issues.</p></li><l=
i style=3D"margin: 8px 0 0 32px;mso-special-format: bullet;unicode-bidi: plai=
ntext;"><p style=3D"color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;margin-bottom: 0;b=
ox-sizing: border-box;padding-left: 4px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plainte=
xt;margin: 0;">The second principle is that the same catalog entries should w=
ork across distinct environments. For example, offline profiling, CI/CD pull =
request checks, and local development tools.</p></li><li style=3D"margin: 8px=
 0 0 32px;mso-special-format: bullet;unicode-bidi: plaintext;"><p style=3D"co=
lor: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;margin-bottom: 0;box-sizing: border-box;=
padding-left: 4px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;margin: 0;">Third, =
you need to format entries so that an automation script can easily inject the=
m into an LLM&#8217;s system prompt.</p></li><li style=3D"margin: 8px 0 0 32p=
x;mso-special-format: bullet;unicode-bidi: plaintext;"><p style=3D"color: rgb=
(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;margin-bottom: 0;box-sizing: border-box;padding-=
left: 4px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;margin: 0;">Lastly, the con=
tents of the catalog should be reviewable by human developers.</p></li></ul><=
p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-siz=
e: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">To implement the Pattern Catalog, the Netfl=
ix engineering team used a simple Git repository filled with plain Markdown f=
iles. They didn&#8217;t use vector databases or complex knowledge stores. The=
 idea was borrowed from the &#8220;LLM-wiki&#8221; concept popularized by And=
rej Karpathy.</p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-hei=
ght: 26px;font-size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">By using a standard Git r=
epository, the developers got several advantages. For one, developers can dif=
f changes, open pull requests, and use git features to find out why an entry =
was created. It also scales well to 100s of detailed performance rules withou=
t the need for complex search infrastructure. Lastly, plain Markdown is easy =
for both humans and language models to read without translation layers.</p><h=
