bidi: plaintext;">In the reactive path, your system profiles production servi=
ces on a recurring schedule or on demand. When the agent finds a new bottlene=
ck, it tests the fix on a canary instance. If everything goes fine, the patch=
 is merged, and the agent documents the new finding in the Pattern Catalog.</=
p><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 20px 0;color: rgb(54,55,55);line-height: 26px;font-=
size: 16px;unicode-bidi: plaintext;">In the proactive path, the process start=
s when a developer creates a new PR. CI tooling performs a fast regex or symb=
ol match against the Pattern Catalog index. If the code in the PR matches kno=
wn anti-patterns, the CI bot calls an LLM and provides it with the pull reque=
st diff. The LLM checks the context and leaves an inline comment that explain=
s the inefficiency. It shows the resource impact and suggests a fix. All this=
 happens before the code ever merges to the main branch.</p><h2 class=3D"head=
